---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The owner experience"
  description="Restless is designed to return prepared outcomes and bounded owner decisions."
  active="product"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <h1>Bring the mission.<br /><em>Leave the machinery.</em></h1>
    <p>Restless is intended to feel like appointing a capable company, not configuring an agent framework. The owner supplies direction, limits, taste and judgement.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="paired-prose">
    <h2>Your working day should have fewer open loops.</h2>
    <div><p>One singleton Exec owns the portfolio and delegates every executable request to one accountable lead. Staff does the machine-doable work. The lead stays available to notice drift, redirect production and inspect the result.</p><p>The return is the native artifact with supporting evidence and one bounded decision where a human boundary remains.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="human-boundary">
    <div><h2>Restless stops at the line only you can cross.</h2><p>Identity, sign-in, CAPTCHA, two-factor authentication, legal attestation, payment confirmation and irreducible taste remain owner acts. The company should prepare everything around them.</p></div>
    <dl class="receipt-sheet">
      <div><dt>Already prepared</dt><dd>Terms compared, quantities checked and a reversible draft preserved.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Your act</dt><dd>Approve the final production order.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Observable resume</dt><dd>The provider's own order state is observed.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="boundary-copy">
    <h2>The target is accountable economic execution.</h2>
    <div class="boundary-rows">
      <p><strong>For</strong> Owner/operators who need work to progress without becoming its project manager.</p>
      <p><strong>Not for</strong> A chat assistant, agent builder, workflow canvas, task tracker or audit product.</p>
      <p><strong>Today</strong> A clean-slate research programme with controlled evidence. No claim of general availability.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
